#
# 11g's reply to it (#2466): the bind prompt (IN, OUT, OUT); then per iteration
# TTI_RXD and, for each target, a ub4 row count and the rows, each the value, a
# ub2 indicator and a ub2 return code: iteration 1 two rows (100, 'abcdef')
# and (101, NULL -- an empty value, -1, 1405), iteration 2 one (200, 'x'),
# iteration 3 none; then the status, three rows.
# Captured 2026-11-06 through tools/capture_proxy.py: an OCI 11.2 program
# (instant client 11.2, x86-64 Linux, the client charset AL32UTF8; an array
# OCIStmtExecute, the RETURNING targets bound OCI_DATA_AT_EXEC with
# OCIBindDynamic, called through ctypes) on Oracle 11g XE 11.2.0.2 with
# SERVER=POOLED, the DRCP pool started, on pyo_drcp_ar (id NUMBER, g NUMBER,
# s VARCHAR2(10)) holding (100, 1, 'abcdef'), (101, 1, NULL), (200, 2, 'x').
# The TTC payload, without the packet's header, as `hexdump -C` output; the
# offset column and the |ascii| gutter are ignored by tests.replay.parse_hexdump.
